{"type":"message","id":"c3e00fd4","parentId":"8621f161","timestamp":"2026-05-18T04:47:14.143Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Hmm, the GET request to /send just returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" and doesn't actually send a message. Maybe the POST endpoint issue is something specific with how Cloudflare Workers handles that route. \n\nThe error 1101 is a Cloudflare Workers error meaning \"No domain\" - that might mean the Worker isn't properly configured or the route doesn't match.\n\nLet me check if there's something specific about the request format. Maybe the POST body needs to include a specific structure.\n\nWait, could the issue be that the worker is returning a 1101 because of the Content-Type header or something? Let me try without Content-Type.\n\nActually, looking at this differently - the GET /send returned \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" - this is probably just the API saying it received the request, not that it sent a message. Maybe the POST is needed but is failing with a Cloudflare error.\n\n\nI should attempt the POST request without the Content-Type header to see if that's causing the routing issue.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-464f4576-734b-4680-b4e2-9f787c17ee02","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"# Try without Content-Type\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-Key: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -d \"threadId=arbitration&content=Heartbeat+04:45+UTC\" 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":786,"output":303,"cacheRead":18816,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19905,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779079615204,"responseId":"chatcmpl-2796062f-d033-4f9c-8e08-63559a7aa654"}}
